// doubt-review — premise library for finalize/doubt_review.
//
// WHEN TO USE: the adversarial pass over the finished plan branch. Model each
// suspicion explicitly and let the engine keep you honest: a bug is only
// proven when reproduced, and "reviewed" is a claim with prerequisites.
// Skip (not_applicable) only if the plan produced no code to doubt.
//
// HOW TO USE (your program):
//   DOMAIN check
//   IMPORT "templates/doubt-review.vrf"
//   FACT doubt_review.review is_complete       // the claim under test
//   // state the outcome of the hunt — exactly one of:
//   NOT  doubt_review.bug proven               // nothing survived probing
//   // ...or, when a bug DID survive:
//   //   FACT doubt_review.bug reproducible
//   //   FACT doubt_review.bug proven
//   //   FACT doubt_review.bug fixed_in_branch   // or recorded_as_followup
//   CHECK BIDIRECTIONAL
// Bind ports via `values`: {"risky_areas_probed": true, ...}.
//
// INLINE RECIPES (copy into YOUR file):
//   // explore a hypothesis without committing (engine backtracks for you):
//   ASSUME cache is stale
//   ASSUME NOT cache invalidated_on_write
//   // separate "the code claims" from "I verified":
//   BELIEVES author retries are_bounded     // false belief -> reported, not fatal
//   KNOWS reviewer tests are_green          // knowing a falsehood -> CONFLICT
//   // probe a candidate conclusion before writing it as FACT:
//   TRY leak is_in_worker
DOMAIN doubt_review

// -- external ports (bind via `values`) --
VAR risky_areas_probed     // each risky area got a dedicated probe
VAR claims_cross_checked   // summary claims were checked against the diff
VAR tests_actually_run     // the final test run happened (not assumed)
VAR no_unrecorded_doubt    // every remaining doubt is written down

// -- the claim: the review is complete --
PREMISE review_needs_probes:
    WHEN review is_complete
    THEN risky_areas_probed
PREMISE review_needs_cross_check:
    WHEN review is_complete
    THEN claims_cross_checked
PREMISE review_needs_test_run:
    WHEN review is_complete
    THEN tests_actually_run
PREMISE review_needs_doubts_recorded:
    WHEN review is_complete
    THEN no_unrecorded_doubt

// -- epistemic discipline: an unreproduced bug is not a proven bug --
RULE unreproduced_is_unproven:
    WHEN NOT bug reproducible
    THEN NOT bug proven
PREMISE proven_needs_repro:
    WHEN bug proven
    THEN bug reproducible

// -- a found bug creates a duty: fix it or file it, never both dropped --
RULE proven_bug_needs_disposition:
    WHEN bug proven
    THEN bug needs_disposition
RULE no_bug_no_disposition:
    WHEN NOT bug proven
    THEN NOT bug needs_disposition
PREMISE disposition_gate:
    WHEN bug needs_disposition
    THEN bug fixed_in_branch
    OR   bug recorded_as_followup
